/**
 * Gap-buffered index array (§4.4).
 *
 * The stream source merge-inserts arriving rows into the existing permutation
 * rather than triggering a full re-sort. For a sorted numeric column that is a
 * binary search plus a splice — and a splice into a plain `Uint32Array` is
 * O(n) memmove per row, which at a million rows and a chunk a frame is the
 * whole cost of streaming.
 *
 * A gap buffer keeps a movable hole at the last insertion point, so a run of
 * insertions near each other — which is what sorted, chunked data produces —
 * costs O(1) amortised each. Reads are one branch and an index adjustment.
 */

/** Slack allocated ahead of the data on construction and on growth. */
const DEFAULT_SLACK = 64;

/**
 * A `Uint32Array` of row indices with a movable gap.
 */
